      "message": "feat(app): a turning tool takes its record and body from linked lathe components\n\nThe document derivation sends a turning tool's component stack to the\ncamcraft-tools lathe resolver (#4194). SetToolAssembly and\nEditDocumentComponent land the Turning record (nose radius, orientation,\ninsert size, the insert's running data) and the lathe-frame body in one\nundo step. A shared insert edit updates every holder that uses it, and\ntheir turning operations go Stale.\n\n- DocumentComponent gets lathe_body (boxes or facets).\n- ResolvedLathe gives the placed facets of its bands.\n- Refused by name: a grooving, threading or form stack, a root that is\n  not a rectangular or round shank, each resolver refusal, and a lathe\n  body in a spindle stack.\n\nRefs #3643\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
